-- 06: capabilities are orthogonal to interpretations — one policy, many
--     targets, and the capability-secure unikernel.
--
-- POC for OCP-0007. NOT compilable today.
--
-- Because capabilities are a separate axis from interpretations, the SAME
-- program and the SAME policy port across a Linux dev box, seL4, bare metal, or
-- a pure test — only the interpretation (who implements the op) changes. The
-- capability grade, inferred and checked, is identical in every case.

signature putLine  : Eff (String Utf8) Unit
signature readFile : Eff (String Utf8) (String Utf8)

-- Orthogonal policy — authored once, reused under every interpretation below.
require putLine  : {Console}
require readFile : {FileRead}

-- The program. Inferred:  (String Utf8) →[{Console, FileRead}] Unit
report : Eff (String Utf8) Unit
report = readFile >>> putLine

-- The interpretation supplies the OPERATIONS; the policy above supplies the
-- CAPABILITIES. They never mention each other. Pick one at link time:
--
--   import I.Linux.File   as Host   -- putLine/readFile via Linux syscalls
--   import I.SeL4.File    as Host   -- via seL4 caps to a file server
--   import I.Test.Capture as Host   -- pure: canned reads, collected writes
--
-- In all three, `report`'s capability grade is the same {Console, FileRead}.

-- ── The capability-secure unikernel ───────────────────────────────────────
--
-- A Once unikernel is `program + interpretation` linked into ONE image; the
-- interpretation stratum IS the OS runtime — there is no kernel/user boundary.
-- Security is enforced at COMPILE TIME (the inferred grade + a type error on
-- under-grant) plus a single ROOT grant at boot. No runtime ambient authority,
-- no syscall check.
--
--   * `main` holds the root capability and attenuates it down to components.
--   * A component without a capability in its grade CANNOT call the operation
--     (type error). Its inferred type is its authority manifest.
--   * Swap I.Linux → I.SeL4 and the very same policy still holds.

signature withConsole  : (Eff[ {Console}  ∪ r ] A B) -> (Eff[ r ] A B)
signature withFileRead : (Eff[ {FileRead} ∪ r ] A B) -> (Eff[ r ] A B)

main : IO Unit
main = withConsole (withFileRead (report "motd.txt"))
